A||||6||fiero_hunter85||which computer do i use?||||1||
Z||000000||fiero_hunter85||10-01-2001||09:20 AM||||very soon i am getting a 2.8 out of a late 80's cavalier that i am going to put in my 85 GT. i am going to put the  fiero intake manifold and plenum on it but i am using the cavalier heads. wich computer do i use the cavalier or fiero comp?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/front_left_2_1.jpg">  85 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-01-2001||09:38 AM||||Use the one for the Fiero.<BR>I'm not 100% certain, but I don't think that you will be able to retain the heads of the Cavalier. I feel that the heads and intake (lower) are different for both engines and you will not be able to use the Fieros intake without swapping heads.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||10-01-2001||10:08 AM||||If they are the cast iron heads you can use them but  WHY.  They have smaller valves and won't breath as well so you'll take a performance hit.  Using the Fiero prom will be close but not perfect so don't expect it to run as well as it could with a matched ecm.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||10-01-2001||12:15 PM||||What year is this Cavalier.  It most likely has Aluminum heads.  You probably can't use the Fiero flywheel Flexplate/flywheel and a bunch of other things. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||10-01-2001||03:11 PM||||87 up Cavaliers got the aluminum heads and DIS ignition. A fiero intake will not fit those heads. If you get an aluminum head engine, you will need the ecm and engine wiring harness for that engine.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero_nightmare||10-01-2001||05:24 PM||||there are about 4 differant engines i have to choose from so i am not sure of the year yet. te fiero heard are MAJORLY gunked up and 3 exhaust manifold bolts are busted off so i want to use the cav heades. i have to get one with a distribitor because that is what my fiero has.||||reg||1
Z||000006||00lE||10-02-2001||04:26 AM||||You cannot swap iron heads onto a block that originally had aluminum heads without also changing the pistons.  The same goes for swapping aluminum heads onto an iron head block.  The aluminum head volume is nearly twice that of the iron head, hence the need for the different pistons.<BR>The Fiero 2.8 intake will not work with the aluminum heads, so you are basically looking at a swap very similar to a 3.8 in difficulty.  Probably not even worth it unless you were to use a late model (&gt;99) 3100/3400 motor that you had obtained for a VERY good price.<BR>Find a Camaro/Firebird 3.4 and use it instead.. You can search the forum to find out what is required to do an iron head 3.4 swap, it is a much simpler swap than any of the fwd alumunum head motors will be.<P><p>[This message has been edited by 00lE (edited 10-02-2001).]||||reg||1
